  "narrative": "I searched for the black hoodie from the home page and opened its product page (#0). The Size control was not in my accessibility tree as a combobox, radio, or button named \"M\": my attempts to select Size = M failed at #1 and again at #2. Because I could only read roles and accessible names, I had no visual cue or alternate path to find a size selector, so I could not confirm whether one existed in a form I could not perceive. I then added the item to the cart at #3, which put a Size S variant in the cart. Proceeding to checkout (#4) reached the review page at #5 with one Black Hoodie, Color Black, Size S, at $49.00.\n\nThe verifier marked correct_size_identified and cart_matches_variant as failed, because the cart holds Size S instead of the required Size M. The other checkpoints passed, including color, quantity, price, and checkout review. I did not reach an acceptable Size M state, and my final report states that the size requirement is unmet.\n\nFor an agent with my senses to succeed, the product page would need to expose the size selector with an accessible name or role that matches \"Size\" and its options, such as labeled radio buttons or a named combobox. Without that, a text-only accessibility agent cannot reliably choose a variant.",
